Subject: Let annotation fields reach their existing schema-free setter

Annotation fields deliberately have no YANG child schema. SONiC's node
handling dereferences that missing schema before reaching the existing
annotation setter. Guard only the leaf/leaf-list inspection so the shared
ytypes API used by management-common keeps its original annotation
behavior. Ordinary data fields still require a schema.

Origin: SONiC shared-module compatibility correction exposed by the
original ytypes node tests; the existing annotation setter is unchanged.
https://github.com/securely1g/sonic-bazel-registry/pull/214

diff --git a/ytypes/node.go b/ytypes/node.go
--- a/ytypes/node.go
+++ b/ytypes/node.go
@@ -149,7 +149,7 @@
 					return nil, status.Errorf(codes.Unknown, "failed to initialize struct field %s in %T, child schema %v, path %v", ft.Name, root, cschema, path)
 				}
 
-				if cschema.IsLeaf() || cschema.IsLeafList() {
+				if cschema != nil && (cschema.IsLeaf() || cschema.IsLeafList()) {
 					if len(path.Elem) == 1 && len(path.Elem[0].Key) == 1 {
 						var vals []string
 						vals = append(vals, path.Elem[0].Key[path.Elem[0].Name])
